 leads the rayon which  is like the main robot faction that  you're fighting but then you play as  this guy called Romer and he leads his  kind of band of outlaws and they're the  ones kind of going around rallying up  humanity to fight against this robot  uprising but you're a robot too right so  Romer is yes Romer himself is a robot so  like the rayon faction is kind of fully  given over to like automation and being  machines and that sort of thing like  their humanity is gone but roamers still  retains some of that and in fact  like part of their goal is to hopefully  one day disintegrate and actually just  be human again to like get rid of the  robot part gotcha and there we are with  the title yeah there you go  so how does that work in actual missions  like who are you fighting against you  know it when we played in the beta we  saw a lot of battles against other grab  cycle teams and it's like a campaign  it's got to be a little different  there's got to be different enemies and  stuff so what are the rayon kind of like  there are different kind of enemies that  you fight for sure and in fact you  actually have this sort of ping ability  where you can highlight enemies in the  environment learn more about them it's  um it's less of a radar and more about  learning about the world as my  understanding because you can also ping  like architecture in different items in  the environment to learn more about the  world but those enemies that you scan  obviously you also fight and there are  different types you know when it comes  to RTS is you can use your imagination  as to the different units right you have  your your heavier guys you have your  quick or smaller units and it's the same  for you and your team the striker class  is like a big mech and he gets a mortar  you have the Ranger which uses more of a  sniper rifle  the sniper also has this thing called a  slow field it slows down your enemies  and their bullets within the field so  you can kind of use that